  "note": "Annual election of six urban councillors, nominations 4 January 1934; six candidates for six vacancies, so there was no contest (Belfast News-Letter, 5 January 1934, p. 7). All but M'Gookin were retiring members; the sixth retiring member, Stanley Heggan, did not seek re-election. Citation unconfirmed: the names were not all found on the cited page (verification 5 Nov 2026). Returned unopposed."
